All right.

60
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:58,450
So the first word that we have or it's actually a concept, minimal landscaping.

61
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:02,030
Okay, so minimal is a style, minimalist actually.

62
00:04:02,350 --> 00:04:08,950
And minimal landscaping is this kind of style of, well, designing your lawn or your garden.

63
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:12,810
So minimal means not having adornments or decorations.

64
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:14,070
Okay.

65
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:17,450
So it's kind of like the less is more type thing.

66
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:17,990
Exactly.

67
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:24,490
So minimal architecture could be very simple, lots of clean lines, not much decoration.

68
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:28,570
It's the opposite of something that's baroque and highly ornamented.

69
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
And I don't like that.

70
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:30,450
I'm into minimal.

71
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,720
All right, minimalist.

72
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,750
Anyways, we have minimal landscaping.

73
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:41,410
And while he's talking about his patio and an old fashioned grill, and he said quaint lawn furniture.

74
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:46,730
Quaint is sometimes, well, it's usually kind of a bad thing.

75
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:56,950
We say something is quaint in the way of saying that it's cute, but we don't really like it because it's maybe old fashioned or kind of old style.

76
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,670
So oh, isn't that quaint?

77
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:04,550
It's something that people from the city often say about people in the country, at least in America.

78
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:09,400
So, oh, because you know, I went to school on the East Coast and I'm from the Midwest.

79
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:19,970
So people on the East Coast would say, oh, your house is so quaint, small and cute and old fashioned because they live in a big fancy New York apartment or whatever.

80
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:24,400
So quaint is usually something that's not the nicest.

81
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:29,050
So he's looking for some lawn furniture that's not like plastic or new.

82
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:30,810
It's more like old fashioned, maybe wood.

83
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,560
Right.

84
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:35,850
And kind of traditional and not fancy.

85
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,800
Kind of simple.

86
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:46,970
Now, he's also talking about the house and he wants, well, a two carport, pastel siding and a gable roof.

87
00:05:47,450 --> 00:05:51,150
So now we know what a roof is, but what is a gable roof?

88
00:05:51,650 --> 00:05:53,930
A gable is a thing, right?

89
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:57,610
And it's almost like an extension of the roof in certain parts.

90
00:05:57,610 --> 00:06:04,350
For example, on a traditional Cape Cod style house, you have windows in the front that they're not a part of the roof.

91
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:05,240
They're an extension.

92
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,640
They come out.

93
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:07,640
They're kind of popping out like eyes.

94
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,640
Exactly.

95
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:09,640
They're coming out like eyes.

96
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,400
And so the roof, obviously you need a roof on top of those windows.

97
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:15,150
So that kind of roof, that little extension, that's called a gable.

98
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:20,650
And so there's a wonderful book that's famous in American history called The House of Seven Gables.

99
00:06:21,370 --> 00:06:25,420
That means that on this roof of the house, there are seven different parts that come out.

100
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:26,580
Seven gables.

101
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:27,360
It's very unique.

102
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:29,540
Those houses usually look a little bit scary.

103
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:30,340
They do.

104
00:06:30,340 --> 00:06:32,620
Victorian and imposing.

105
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:33,580
All right.

106
00:06:34,180 --> 00:06:35,280
So you have a gable roof.

107
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,360
Now you have shutters and a white picket fence.

108
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:40,530
This is typical.

109
