248
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:01,560
Yeah.

249
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:08,260
And so these are all words you can use, names you could use with men and women, but buttercup is mostly women.

250
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:11,360
I think the other ones are more general.

251
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:16,380
But do you think like, do guys say to their loved ones like, sweetum, sweetie pie?

252
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,040
Oh, yeah.

253
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,040
Yeah?

254
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:19,710
Oh, yeah.

255
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:21,040
All right.

256
00:12:21,570 --> 00:12:27,710
So I guess guys, if you want to be really sweet and you want to win over the hearts of the ladies, you can use these words as well.

257
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:32,290
Another popular one is babe, which is more of a young person thing to say.

258
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,320
Yeah, I think it's more modern as well.

259
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,010
Honey or babe?

260
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:36,830
Baby.

261
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:38,280
Baby.

262
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:40,280
You're verging on not so sweet.

263
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:42,020
Yeah, but like, hey, baby, how are you?

264
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,480
It's like, nice.

265
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,480
But not like, hey, baby.

266
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,480
All right.

267
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:49,780
Well, we're going to leave you with that thought and go listen to this dialogue one more time.

268
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,160
We'll be back in a moment.

269
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:02,380
Mr. and Mrs. Robinson, let's get straight to it.

270
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:06,860
You have saved up your money for years and are now ready to build your dream home.

271
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:08,380
What did you have in mind?

272
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:11,540
A suburban bungalow straight out of the 60s.

273
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:18,960
A perfect lawn with minimal landscaping, a brick patio in the backyard with an old-fashioned grill, quaint lawn furniture, and a swimming pool.

274
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:25,860
A two-car carport, pastel siding, and a gable roof, completed with white shutters and a white picket fence.

275
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,290
Uh, honey?

276
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:33,430
In the living room, we would have moss green rugs and a fireplace with a stone mantle and wood paneling on the walls.

277
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:39,930
In the kitchen, the cupboards would be a pale yellow, and we would have a turquoise metal oven and vinyl flooring.

278
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:47,510
Um, sweetie, but I was thinking of more a modern-style house, an open-concept house all glass, wood, metal, and concrete.

279
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:52,860
But sweetums, there's always a lot of wasted space in those kinds of homes.

280
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,780
Besides, it's just a fad.

281
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:57,560
It doesn't have the homey feeling the old homes do.

282
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,160
Sweetie pie, it's not a lot of wasted space.

283
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:08,760
It is relaxing, and the house would be eco-friendly with an in-floor heating system and designed to retain the heat of the sun in the winter and keep the house cool in the summer.

284
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,880
We would have solar panels on the roof.

285
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:13,120
Do you know how much those things cost?

286
00:14:13,890 --> 00:14:16,170
What about your vintage furniture, dearest?

287
00:14:16,650 --> 00:14:27,250
And instead of a lawn, which is also a lot of wasted space and would require environmentally harmful pesticides, we would have a fish pond in the backyard and a garden that would cover the whole yard so we could grow our own food.

288
00:14:27,710 --> 00:14:31,990
But Buttercup, I thought you always said that you loved visiting your grandmother's house.

289
00:14:32,590 --> 00:14:38,170
And I thought you, Mr. Scientist, were all up on saving the planet with your technological advancements.

290
00:14:38,810 --> 00:14:43,470
Um, well, I am just going to get some coffee while you two keep discussing.

291
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:50,760
Alright we're back.

292
00:14:51,160 --> 00:15:05,000
So apart from this decorations and stuff, do you agree with the vintage home, the more like minimalist thing, or do you like the open concept one, the bigger one?

293
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:11,040
I love the look of minimalism, but as a place to live, it's not comfortable.

294
00:15:11,040 --> 00:15:24,560
And so when I think of an aesthetic that I like, a look that I like, I really like kind of dark wood, velvety, 19th century kind of, I think of old Vienna.

295
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:25,320
You like Castle Dracula.

296
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:26,800
No, not dark.

297
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,220
I like things to be open.

298
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:38,280
And I like a lot of natural light, but I also like oversized kind of heavy furniture and really luscious fabrics and things like that.

299
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:39,480
So that's my...

300
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:42,900
I'm actually completely different because I do like this open concept.

301
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:52,560
I like those houses that, I like the way they look inside as well as outside when they're kind of squared, big windows, clean lines.

302
00:15:52,560 --> 00:16:04,970
Inside is like, for example, in the kitchen you have polished aluminum or polished steel furniture in the kitchen, as well as a lot of white and red or black, especially.

303
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,770
I kind of like that kind of open spaces.

304
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:09,800
Primary colors.

305
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:10,920
Yeah, yeah.

306
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:13,160
Flat screen TVs on the wall and stuff like that.

307
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:13,920
Remote controls.

308
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:14,860
Ikea lamps.

309
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:22,300
Yeah, you know, like those remote controls where you can open your curtains, your TV and the lights all at the same time.

310
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:23,480
I kind of like that stuff.

311
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:23,640
Cool.

312
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:28,520
Well, let us know what you guys like because everyone has their own opinion on what a beautiful house is.

313
00:16:29,080 --> 00:16:32,440
And if you have any pictures, feel free to share them with us on our website, EnglishPod.com.

314
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:33,180
All right.

315
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:33,800
We'll see you guys there.

316
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:35,440
Bye.
